  "template": {
    "en": "Pushing a piston forward in a tube of air makes a region packed closer than average, called a {a}. Pulling it back makes a region more spread out than average, called a {b}. A series of these regions travelling through a medium, while the particles only vibrate about their own places, is a {c}. A wave that needs a medium to travel is a {d}. Sound is one; light is not."
