  "explanation": {
    "en": "A region packed closer than average is a compression, and a region more spread out than average is a rarefaction. A series of compressions and rarefactions travelling through a medium is a sound wave. A sound wave needs particles to pass the vibration on, so it is a mechanical wave. Light is not a mechanical wave: it can cross a vacuum."
  },
